tags: blake2b-trailing-zeros, blake2b

A proof of work: find a solution so that the BLAKE2b-512 hash of the challenge and the
solution ends with d zero characters in lowercase hexadecimal, where d is the
difficulty.

The input of the hash is the UTF-8 of the challenge, then the UTF-8 of the solution,
with nothing between. The hash is BLAKE2b with a 64-byte digest, no key, no salt and no
personalization. Its lowercase hexadecimal has 128 characters. The difficulty is the
number of characters, from 0 to 64. Each character is 4 bits of work.

The node asks for it in PoWRequired. The caller does the work.

=== formal
class=proof-of-work
difficulty=d, the number of hexadecimal characters, 0 to 64
hash.type=786a02f742015903c6c6fd852552d272912f4740e15847618a86e217f71f5419d25e1031afee585313896444934eb04b903a685b1448b755d56f701afe9be2ce
input=UTF-8 of the challenge, then UTF-8 of the solution, with nothing between
name=blake2b-trailing-zeros
rule=the lowercase hexadecimal of the hash ends with d characters '0'
unit=hexadecimal character (4 bits)
